THOUGHT: compressedData is annotated @Nullable and checked for null in other methods (e.g., consumeCustomData), but getData(int,int) dereferences it without a check. To satisfy NullAway and be consistent with the API (getData is @Nullable and can return null), I should add a null check at the start of getData that returns null if compressedData is null. This avoids NPEs and doesn’t change behavior for valid prepared states. After editing, I’ll run the Gradle compile to confirm the NullAway error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '368,389s/@Nullable
  public ByteBuffer getData(int requestedLevel, int requestedFace) {/@Nullable
  public ByteBuffer getData(int requestedLevel, int requestedFace) {
    if (compressedData == null) {
      return null;
    }/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/glutils/KTXTextureData.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway:.*errors" -n new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log```

